1. DEFINITIONS

"Private Repository" means this non-public SEAM development repository,
including its source code, specifications, schemas, documentation, tests,
benchmarks, fixtures, designs, research, models, data, build and release
tooling, history, and other materials.

"Reserved Materials" means all material in the Private Repository that is not
expressly identified in writing by the Project Owner as carrying another
license.

"MIRL Reserved Materials" means the copyrighted expression and non-public
implementation materials relating to MIRL, including specifications, schemas,
records, compilation, extraction, grounding, normalization, reconciliation,
storage, indexing, retrieval, graph projection, vectorization, provenance,
PACK, symbol-table and improvement-loop machinery, compression, and codecs.

"HS/1 Reserved Materials" means the copyrighted expression and non-public
implementation materials relating to SEAM-HS/1 Holographic Surfaces, including
specifications, container expression, visual designs, codecs, surface
libraries, compilation, encoding, decoding, verification, repair, storage,
query, rendering, and provenance.

"SEAM-U Reserved Materials" means any non-public SEAM-U weights, checkpoints,
optimizer state, tokenizer, training or alignment code, data mixture,
annotations, prompts, evaluations, inference implementation, and related model
artifacts developed or controlled by the Project Owner.

"Authorized Contributor" means a person whom the Project Owner has expressly
authorized in writing to access the Private Repository for work on SEAM.

"Legacy Apache Materials" means only exact file versions previously published
under the Apache License, Version 2.0. The public repository and artifact
history identifies those versions.

"Historical Source-Available Releases" means only exact artifacts previously
published under the Business Source License 1.1 or another source-available
license. The artifact's own license, version, manifest, and publication record
identify those releases.

